#### {{ sec.reach }} How far this reaches beyond one child

The readthrough axis is not specific to this child's allele. Of the {{ cv.pathogenic_total }} {{ domain_map.gene }} variants classified pathogenic or likely pathogenic in ClinVar {{ params.clinvar_release }}, **{{ cv.truncating }} ({{ cv.truncating_pct }}%) are nonsense or frameshift** ({{ cv.nonsense }} nonsense, {{ cv.frameshift }} frameshift), with {{ cv.splice }} splice-affecting and {{ cv.other }} other, counted from the same ClinVar release this pipeline uses for annotation. A readthrough strategy is relevant to any patient carrying at least one nonsense allele, so it addresses a substantial share of the pathogenic alleles reported in this gene rather than a single private variant.

The method generalises further than the gene does. Characterising the stop codon and its 3′ context, predicting the near-cognate products and scoring them, gating aminoglycosides on MT-RNR1, and flagging phenotype-dependent contraindications are all disease-agnostic steps; they apply to any recessive disorder with a nonsense allele. Each is a pipeline step rather than a manual lookup, so the same analysis runs on another genome unchanged; the steps are named in the provenance section.
